\title{Cut capacity}
\date{2026-11-16T18:41:20Z}
\tag{algorithms}

\import{algorithms-macros}

\taxon{Definition}
\p{The \em{capacity} of an #{s}-#{t} cut, denoted #{c(A,B)}, is the total capacity of all edges crossing the cut. That is, ##{c(A,B) = \sum_{e : A \to B} c(e).} (The notation #{e : A \to B} denotes any edge which goes from some vertex in #{A} to some vertex in #{B}.)}
